{"id":"marco-polo","title":"The Travels of Marco Polo","who":"Marco Polo, with his father and uncle","when":"1271–1295","vehicle":"On foot, horse and camel caravans; home by sea","kind":"other","color":"#92400e","summary":"A young Venetian sets out with his merchant father and uncle along the Silk Road to the court of Kublai Khan, serves him for years, and returns by sea through Southeast Asia and India. His book opened Asia to European imagination for centuries.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Marco Polo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Polo"}],"approximate":"Historians reconstruct the route from the book; places are approximate and some are debated. Drawn on today's roads and sea lanes.","km":28431,"bbox":[12.3346,5.179,118.6724,45.4372],"stops":[{"name":"Venice","place":"Venice, Italy","at":[45.4372,12.3346],"date":"1271","text":"Seventeen-year-old Marco leaves Venice with his father Niccolò and uncle Maffeo, who had already been to China.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Venezia_aerial_view.jpg/500px-Venezia_aerial_view.jpg","page":"Venice","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venezia_aerial_view.jpg","credit":"kallerna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Acre","place":"Acre, Israel","at":[32.9282,35.0756],"text":"By ship across the Mediterranean to the crusader port of Acre.","by":"boat"},{"name":"Ayas","place":"Ayas","at":[36.77,35.79],"text":"Landing at Ayas, a busy trading port, to start overland.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Yumurtal%C4%B1k_town_2987.jpg/500px-Yumurtal%C4%B1k_town_2987.jpg","page":"Yumurtalık","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yumurtal%C4%B1k_town_2987.jpg","credit":"Dosseman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tabriz","place":"Tabriz, Iran","at":[38.0739,46.2979],"text":"A great trading city of Persia, full of merchants from everywhere.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg/500px-Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg","page":"Tabriz","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg","credit":"user:Elmju","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kerman","place":"Kerman, Iran","at":[29.5719,57.301],"text":"South across Persia towards the sea."},{"name":"Hormuz","place":"Hormuz","at":[27.07,56.46],"text":"They hoped to sail from Hormuz, judged the ships unsafe, and turned back overland.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Iran%27s_Rainbow_Island.jpeg/500px-Iran%27s_Rainbow_Island.jpeg","page":"Hormuz Island","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iran%27s_Rainbow_Island.jpeg","credit":"NASA Earth Observatory image by Lauren Dauphin, using Landsat data from the U.S. Geological Survey. Story by Adam Voilan","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Balkh","place":"Balkh, Afghanistan","at":[36.7581,66.898],"text":"The ancient \"mother of cities\", still in ruins after the Mongol conquest.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Green_Mosque%2C_Balkh.jpg/500px-Green_Mosque%2C_Balkh.jpg","page":"Balkh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Mosque%2C_Balkh.jpg","credit":"AhmadElhan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Badakhshan & the Pamirs","place":"Ishkashim, Afghanistan","at":[36.8539,71.4632],"text":"Over the high Pamirs, where Marco describes great wild sheep, later named after him.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Wakhan.png/500px-Wakhan.png","page":"Wakhan Corridor","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wakhan.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kashgar","place":"Kashgar, China","at":[39.4666,75.99],"text":"An oasis town at the western end of the Taklamakan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/H%C3%ABytgah_Mosque%2C_Kashi_%2820230923100109%29.jpg/500px-H%C3%ABytgah_Mosque%2C_Kashi_%2820230923100109%29.jpg","page":"Kashgar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%ABytgah_Mosque%2C_Kashi_%2820230923100109%29.jpg","credit":"N509FZ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Khotan","place":"Hotan, China","at":[37.111,79.9209],"text":"Along the southern edge of the desert, famous for jade.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Kurban_Tulum_with_Mao_Zedong%2C_Hotan%2C_China.jpg/500px-Kurban_Tulum_with_Mao_Zedong%2C_Hotan%2C_China.jpg","page":"Hotan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurban_Tulum_with_Mao_Zedong%2C_Hotan%2C_China.jpg","credit":"Yoshi Canopus","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Lop desert","place":"Lop desert","at":[39.02,88.17],"text":"A month-long desert crossing, with tales of spirit voices luring travellers away.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Taklamakan_desert.jpg/500px-Taklamakan_desert.jpg","page":"Taklamakan Desert","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taklamakan_desert.jpg","credit":"Pravit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Dunhuang","place":"Dunhuang, China","at":[40.1411,94.6608],"text":"Into China proper at the edge of the desert.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Jiucenglou_of_Mogao_Caves.jpg/500px-Jiucenglou_of_Mogao_Caves.jpg","page":"Mogao Caves","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jiucenglou_of_Mogao_Caves.jpg","credit":"慕尼黑啤酒","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Shangdu (Xanadu)","place":"Shangdu (Xanadu)","at":[42.36,116.18],"text":"Kublai Khan's summer capital, where they are received in 1275.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Yuan_Shangdu.jpg/500px-Yuan_Shangdu.jpg","page":"Shangdu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuan_Shangdu.jpg","credit":"Flaumfeder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Khanbaliq (Beijing)","place":"Beijing, China","at":[39.9057,116.3913],"text":"Years in the Khan's service, sent on missions across his empire.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/The_Beijing_Gulou.JPG/500px-The_Beijing_Gulou.JPG","page":"Dadu (Beijing)","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Beijing_Gulou.JPG","credit":"Bergmann","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Zaiton (Quanzhou)","place":"Quanzhou, China","at":[24.8755,118.6724],"text":"They finally leave, escorting a Mongol princess by sea to Persia.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/20230130_Old_City_of_Quanzhou_01.jpg/500px-20230130_Old_City_of_Quanzhou_01.jpg","page":"Quanzhou","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20230130_Old_City_of_Quanzhou_01.jpg","credit":"Windmemories","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Sumatra","place":"Lhokseumawe, Indonesia","at":[5.179,97.1481],"text":"Months in Sumatra waiting for the monsoon winds.","by":"boat"},{"name":"Sri Lanka","place":"Colombo, Sri Lanka","at":[6.9389,79.8542],"text":"Across the Bay of Bengal, then along the coast of India.","by":"boat"},{"name":"Hormuz","place":"Hormuz","at":[27.07,56.46],"text":"Back in Persia by sea, two years after leaving China.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Strait_of_Hormuz_and_Musandam_Peninsula_%28MODIS_2018-12-10%29.jpg/500px-Strait_of_Hormuz_and_Musandam_Peninsula_%28MODIS_2018-12-10%29.jpg","page":"Strait of Hormuz","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strait_of_Hormuz_and_Musandam_Peninsula_%28MODIS_2018-12-10%29.jpg","credit":"MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Trebizond","place":"Trabzon, Turkey","at":[41.0055,39.7301],"text":"Overland to the Black Sea.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Trebisonda%2C_ex-chiesa_della_panagia_Chrysokephalos%2C_oggi_moschea_fatih%2C_esterno_01.jpg/500px-Trebisonda%2C_ex-chiesa_della_panagia_Chrysokephalos%2C_oggi_moschea_fatih%2C_esterno_01.jpg","page":"Trabzon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trebisonda%2C_ex-chiesa_della_panagia_Chrysokephalos%2C_oggi_moschea_fatih%2C_esterno_01.jpg","credit":"Francesco Bini","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Venice","place":"Venice, Italy","at":[45.4372,12.3346],"date":"1295","text":"Home after 24 years, then captured in a sea war with Genoa, where he dictates his book in prison.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/View_of_the_Grand_Canal_from_Rialto_to_Ca%27Foscari.jpg/500px-View_of_the_Grand_Canal_from_Rialto_to_Ca%27Foscari.jpg","page":"Grand Canal (Venice)","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_the_Grand_Canal_from_Rialto_to_Ca%27Foscari.jpg","credit":"Didier Descouens","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"boat","km":2390,"line":[[45.4372,12.3346],[43.2257,17.7792],[41.7814,20.8521],[40.259,23.786],[38.6657,26.5879],[37.0086,29.2655],[35.2939,31.8268],[32.9282,35.0756]]},{"by":"boat","km":432,"line":[[32.9282,35.0756],[36.77,35.79]]},{"by":"ride","km":1182,"line":[[36.7699,35.7899],[36.8266,35.7895],[36.8642,35.8376],[36.8873,35.8428],[36.9295,35.8465],[36.9905,35.8236],[36.9825,35.8869],[37.0384,36.0888],[37.0855,36.1336],[37.1176,36.2843],[37.1578,36.355],[37.2005,36.3909],[37.1767,36.4636],[37.1896,36.6045],[37.1638,36.6841],[37.2001,36.7306],[37.1828,36.8007],[37.2276,36.8839],[37.2409,37.0123],[37.2864,37.1276],[37.2709,37.2139],[37.2368,37.2672],[37.2098,37.2672],[37.1612,37.3793],[37.1124,37.4063],[37.0651,37.4938],[37.0544,37.6403],[37.0342,37.6743],[37.0282,37.8202],[37.034,37.8778],[37.0746,37.9742],[37.0774,38.081],[37.1065,38.1387],[37.0994,38.192],[37.1296,38.4631],[37.2484,38.6559],[37.2692,38.7959],[37.2621,38.8489],[37.1992,38.9077],[37.2012,38.961],[37.1857,39.0079],[37.1594,39.0152],[37.147,39.1086],[37.1775,39.1918],[37.2303,39.2313],[37.2111,39.547],[37.2308,39.7075],[37.2243,40.0221],[